  partName: Bolt (11)
  description: The Bolt (11) is another tiny, complex-shaped fastener situated at
    the top-center-rear of the engine, working in conjunction with other bolts to
    ensure the engine's components remain securely fastened. Its elongated shape
    allows it to fit into tight spaces, and its Material.001 composition provides
    excellent corrosion resistance. Notably, the Bolt (11) is nearly identical to
    the Bolt (10), highlighting the engine's modular design.
